{
    "name": "Gazowy palnik",
    "category": "tfg:craftsmanship",
    "icon": "tfg:gas_burner",
    "pages": [
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "anchor": "intro",
            "title": "Gazowy palnik",
            "text": "A $(thing)Gas Burner$() is a device which can burn fluids and gases like $(thing)Oil$(), $(l:cooking/alcohol)Alcohol$(), and $(thing)Petroluem Fuels$() to generate $(l:game_mechanics/heating)Heat$().$(br)Unlike other heat sources, the maximum Temperature of the burner can be set using $(l:craftsmanship/gas_burner#redstone)Redstone$(). This allows for more precise control over $(l:cooking/cooking_methods)Cooking$() and $(l:craftsmanship/crucible)Smelting$().$(br)The gas burner does not increase in temperature from a $(l:craftsmanship/charcoal_forge#bellows)Bellows'$() air supply."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:multiblock",
            "multiblock": {
                "pattern": [
                    [
                        "X"
                    ],
                    [
                        "0"
                    ]
                ],
                "mapping": {
                    "X": "tfg:gas_burner[lit=true]"
                }
            },
            "name": "Gazowy palnik",
            "text": "$(thing)Palniki gazowe$() pokazują maksymalną temperaturę na wskaźniku na jednej ze ścianek.",
            "enable_visualize": false
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "anchor": "redstone",
            "title": "Kontrola redstone",
            "text": "This device has many functions that can be controlled with $(bold)$(c)Redstone$():$(li)Supplying a signal strength of $(3)15$() will $(italic)ignite$() the burner.$(li)Removing all redstone signals will $(italic)extinguish$() the burner.$(li)The $(italic)maximum temperature$() of the burner can be set by supplying redstone with signals between $(3)3-14$().$(li)Comparator output will read the current $(italic)fuel level$()."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "anchor": "functions",
            "title": "Funkcje",
            "text": "Gas Burners can be supplied automatically using $(thing)Fluid Pipes$(), or manually with $(item)$(k:key.use)$() while holding a container of fluid.$(br)Inside their interface will show:$(li)The heat level, with a bar indicating maximum set temperature.$(li)A flame progress bar which displays the time left, and fuel burn temp when hovered over.$(li)Fuel tank with bucket in/out slots."
        },
        {
            "type": "patchouli:text",
            "text": "Burners have many useful applications. You can use them for any device which can be supplied with heat from the bottom, such as $(l:craftsmanship/crucible)Crucibles$(), $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#grill)Grills$(), $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#pot)Pots$(), and $(l:cooking/cooking_methods#top_oven)Ovens$(), as well as any Create mechanical machines that need a heat source."
        },
        {
